  <result type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Media outlets and young media workers in Ukraine acquire knowledge and professional experience to produce content that informs and reflects the 
experiences of young people and meets standards of diversity, gender-sensitivity and professional ethics</narrative>
   </title>
   <reference code="271185" vocabulary="99"></reference>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">% of twinnings and co&#x2010;productions resulting in media broadcasting or publishing products in Ukraine</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="2%"></target>
     <actual value="2%"></actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="Collaboration established between Hromadske TV and Danish TV resulting in
media broadcasting or publishing."></target>
     <actual value="The twinning with DR and the new formats were a central part of Hromadske&#x2019;s transformation
from flow TV to online media. 

During phase II, Hromadske achieved the highest percentage of
audience involvement in the content compared to all European players &#x2014; 46%

During phase III, Hromadske reached 46,300 subscribers with an average between 1.7
to 2.0 million views /month. The audiences are 65% women.

A Series of five short documentaries on Covid-19 was produced and broadcasted. Four women and three men. The series reached an audience of 160,000 people of
which 46,000 were quality and deep views. These audiences cannot be disaggregated by gender."></actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="Will be reported on after project ends."></target>
     <actual value="Will be reported on after project ends."></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Young people organise themselves democratically and are active participants in the Ukrainian society in and through media.</narrative>
   </title>
   <reference code="271184" vocabulary="99"></reference>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Level of organised youth actions in and through media indicated through pre&#x2010; and post&#x2010;surveys with key informants.</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="At least 60 % of the surveyed individuals report that the project has contributed to young people&#x2019;s ability to organise themselves 
democratically and to be active participants in the Ukrainian society in and through media."></target>
     <actual value="The original targets of measuring impact and outcome were formulated as quantifiable. Given the changes
in the project following the war and Covid-19, it was deemed more feasible to measure impact through
behavioural change as demonstrated and indicated by partners through dialogue, rather than partner
surveys.

The UPLOAD
project has contributed to the overall objective of countering the lack of youth participation by supporting young people in organising
themselves democratically and becoming active participants in Ukrainian society in and through media."></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
